# Notes\n\nThe authors declare no conflict of interest.\n\n### Citations\n\nCitation\n\ntext copied [Button: Copy]\n\nSteward KF, Payne D, Kincannon W, Johnson C, Lensing M, Fausset H, Németh B, Shepard EM, Broderick WE, Broderick JB, Dubois J, Bothner B. 2022. Proteomic Analysis of Methanococcus voltae Grown in the Presence of Mineral and Nonmineral Sources of Iron and Sulfur. Microbiol Spectr 10:e01893-22.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1128/spectrum.01893-22--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTA-Based Single Event Transient Propagation in Advanced Technology Nodes (https://zenodo.org/records/20511417)\nciteturn43search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: yesterday;     10.5281/zenodo.20511417\n\nDOI\n    Image: Get the DOI badge!\n\nDOI Badge\n\n#### DOI\n\n#### \n    \n    10.5281/zenodo.20511417\n\n### Markdown\n    \n    [![DOI](https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.20511417.svg)](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20511417)\n\n### reStructuredText\n    \n    .. image:: https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.20511417.svg\n      :target: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20511417\n\n### HTML\n    \n    <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20511417\"><img src=\"https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.20511417.svg\" alt=\"DOI\"></a>\n\n### Image URL\n    \n    https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.20511417.svg\n\n### Target URL\n    \n    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20511417\n\nResource type\n    Conference paper\n\nCreated\n    June 2, 2026\n\nModified\n    June 2, 2026--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://journals.asm.org/doi/reader/metadata/10.1128/spectrum.01893-22)\nciteturn43search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.3 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; ###### ARTICLE ... https://doi.org/10.1128/spectrum.01893-22open_in_new\nMicrobiology Spectrum\n\nVolume 10, Issue 4\n\nAug 2022\n\n###### ARTICLE\n\nProteomic Analysis of Methanococcus voltae Grown in the Presence of Mineral and Nonmineral Sources of Iron and Sulfur\n\nView article page\n\nKatherine F. Steward, Devon Payne, Will Kincannon, Christina Johnson, Malachi Lensing, Hunter Fausset, Brigitta Németh, Eric M. Shepard, William E. Broderick, Joan B. Broderick, Jen Dubois, Brian Bothner\n\nCopyright © 2022 Steward et al.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1128/spectrum.01893-22open_in_new\n\nPublisher American Society for Microbiology\n\neISSN 2165-0497\n\nReceived May 24, 2022\n\nAccepted June 17, 2022\n\nOnline July 25, 2022\n\nPublished in issue August 31, 2022\n\neLocator e01893-22\n\nPages 18\n\n## ABSTRACT\n\nIron sulfur (Fe-S) proteins are essential and ubiquitous across all domains of life, yet the mechanisms underpinning assimilation of iron (Fe) and sulfur (S) and biogenesis of Fe-S clusters are poorly understood. This is particularly true for anaerobic methanogenic archaea, which are known to employ more Fe-S proteins than other prokaryotes. Here, we utilized a deep proteomics analysis of Methanococcus voltae A3 cultured in the presence of either synthetic pyrite (FeS_{2}) or aqueous forms of ferrous iron and sulfide to elucidate physiological responses to growth on mineral or nonmineral sources of Fe and S. The liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (LCMS) shotgun proteomics analysis included 77% of the predicted proteome. Through a comparative analysis of intra- and extracellular proteomes, candidate proteins associated with FeS_{2} reductive dissolution, Fe and S acquisition, and the subsequent transport, trafficking, and storage of Fe and S were identified. The proteomic response shows a large and balanced change, suggesting that M. voltae makes physiological adjustments involving a range of biochemical processes based on the available nutrient source. Among the proteins differentially regulated were members of core methanogenesis, oxidoreductases, membrane proteins putatively involved in transport, Fe-S binding ferredoxin and radical S-adenosylmethionine proteins, ribosomal proteins, and intracellular proteins involved in Fe-S cluster assembly and storage. This work improves our understanding of ancient biogeochemical processes and can support efforts in biomining of minerals.\n\nIMPORTANCE Clusters of iron and sulfur are key components of the active sites of enzymes that facilitate microbial conversion of light or electrical energy into chemical bonds. The proteins responsible for transporting iron and sulfur into cells and assembling these elements into metal clusters are not well understood. Using a microorganism that has an unusually high demand for iron and sulfur, we conducted a global investigation of cellular proteins and how they change based on the mineral forms of iron and sulfur. Understanding this process will answer questions about life on early earth and has application in biomining and sustainable sources of energy.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEXECUTIVO\nRepública Federativa do Brasil - Estado (https://forcainvicta.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/doe_2021-10-28_completo.pdf)\nciteturn43search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; 20511417  | VITA MANUELA DOS\nsuas atribuições, resolve designar MARIA APARECIDA DE OLIVEIRA MACHADO, matrícula \nnº 12617029, para, em razão de Licença Premio no período de 21 de Junho de 2021 a 18 de \nSetembro de 2021, substituir PAULO CESAR DOS SANTOS, matrícula nº 20527411, no cargo \nCoordenador III, do(a) CORREGEDORIA DA POLÍCIA CIVIL.\nMatrícula  | Nome  | Cargo  | Símbolo  | Unidade Organizacional  | Data Início\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n20511417  | VITA MANUELA DOS\nSANTOS MUINHOS  | Coordenador\nIV  | DAI-5  | ACADEMIA DA POLÍCIA\nCIVIL  | 30.09.2021RICARDO CESAR MANDARINO BARRETTO\nSECRETARIA DA SEGURANÇA PÚBLICA\n<#E.G.B#591640#42#642856/>\n<#E.G.B#591641#42#642857>\nPortaria Nº 00339679 de 27 de Outubro de 2021\nO(A) SECRETÁRIO(A) DE ESTADO do(a) SECRETARIA DA SEGURANÇA PÚBLICA - SSP, \nno uso das suas atribuições, resolve exonerar, ex officio, o(s) servidor(es) abaixo relacionado(s), \ncom base no(a) art. 44, I, e art. 47, da Lei nº 6.677, de 26 de setembro de 1994:\nHELOISA CAMPOS DE BRITO\nPOLÍCIA CIVIL DO ESTADO DA BAHIA\n<#E.G.B#591530#42#642744/>\n<#E.G.B#591532#42#642748>\nPortaria Nº 00308576 de 27 de Outubro de 2021\nO(A) Delegado Geral do(a) POLÍCIA CIVIL DO ESTADO DA BAHIA - P.CIVIL, no uso de \nsuas atribuições, resolve designar ROGERIO SA MEDRADO, matrícula nº 20410487, para, em \nrazão de Férias no período de 02 de Março de 2020 a 31 de Março de 2020, substituir FILIPE \nFREIRE BEZERRA, matrícula nº 12616398, no cargo Delegado Titular I, do(a) DELEGACIA \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEvaluasi Kinerja Bundaran Tugu Kartasura Menggunakan Studi Mikrosimulasi Lalu Lintas (https://dspace.uii.ac.id/handle/123456789/54888)\nciteturn43search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; 20511417.pdf (5.076Mb)\n\n## Evaluasi Kinerja Bundaran Tugu Kartasura Menggunakan Studi Mikrosimulasi Lalu Lintas\n\nImage: Thumbnail\n\n##### View/Open\n\n20511417.pdf (5.076Mb)\n\n##### Date\n\n2025\n\n##### Author\n\nYudhajakti, Abimanyu Ditya\n\n##### Metadata\n\nShow full item record\n\n##### Abstract\n\nBundaran Tugu Kartasura merupakan titik penting karena terletak di jalur utama yang menghubungkan Kota Solo, Kabupaten Sukoharjo, Kabupaten Karanganyar, serta titik temu antara Kota Yogyakarta dan Kota Semarang. Kondisi lalu lintas di Bundaran Tugu Kartasura dapat berubah tergantung pada waktu dan hari tertentu, tetapi karena merupakan titik penting dalam sistem transportasi bundaran ini seringkali padat dengan banyaknya kendaraan yang melintas, terutama pada jam sibuk seperti pulang pergi kerja atau akhir pekan. Penelitian ini bertujuan untuk mengidentifikasi kinerja dari Bundaran Tugu Kartasura, mengembangkan model mikrosimulasi lalu lintas serta memberikan alternatif yang dapat dilakukan untuk meningkatkan kinerja bundaran dengan perhitungan PKJI 2023 dan disimulasikan atau dimodelkan menggunakan software PTV VISSIM. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nData Pendidikan Kemendikdasmen (https://referensi.data.kemdikbud.go.id/tabs.php?npsn=20511417)\nciteturn43search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.1 years ago; Crawled: 1.3 years ago;    | NPSN  | :  | 20511417\n\n#### SD NEGERI 2 KARANGANYAR\n\n[Input] Identitas Satuan Pendidikan\n\n     | Nama  | :  | SD NEGERI 2 KARANGANYAR\n   | NPSN  | :  | 20511417\n   | Alamat  | :  | Rt. 04 Rw. 09 Dsn. Banar\n   | Desa/Kelurahan  | :  | KARANGANYAR\n   | Kecamatan/Kota (LN)  | :  | KEC. KEBONAGUNG\n   | Kab.-Kota/Negara (LN)  | :  | KAB. PACITAN\n   | Propinsi/Luar Negeri (LN)  | :  | PROV. JAWA TIMUR\n   | Status Sekolah  | :  | NEGERI\n   | Bentuk Pendidikan  | :  | SD\n   | Jenjang Pendidikan  | :  | DIKDAS\n\n[Input] Dokumen dan Perijinan\n\n     | Kementerian Pembina  | :  | Kementerian Pendidikan Dasar dan Menengah\n     | Naungan  | :  | Pemerintah Daerah\n     | NPYP  | :  | -\n   | No. SK. Pendirian  | :  | PERATURAN BUPATI PACITAN NO. 29 TAHUN 2018\n   | Tanggal SK. Pendirian  | :  | 18-03-2018\n   | Nomor SK Operasional  | :  | PERATURAN BUPATI PACITAN NO. 29 TAHUN 2018\n   | Tanggal SK Operasional  | :  | 18-03-2018\n   | File SK Operasional ()  | :  | Lihat SK Operasional\n   | Tanggal Upload SK Op.  | :  | 22-10-2018 09:23:27\n   | Akreditasi  | :  | B\n\n[Input] Sarana dan Prasarana\n\n     | Luas Tanah  | :  | 1.428 m^{2}\n   | Akses Internet  | :  | 1. -\n |  | :  | 2. 30 Mb\n   | Sumber Listrik  | :  | PLN\n\n[Input] Kontak\n\n     | Fax  | :  | -\n     | Telepon  | :  | \n   | Email  | :  | sdnkaranganyar220511417@gmail.com\n   | Website  | :  | \n   | Operator  | :  | Aris Widyanto\n\n[Input] Peta\n\nLintang: -8.237600000000\nBujur: 111.160200000000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<table id=\"e1\"> 